# eGFR target schema -- SULO 0.2.12 SOLID quantity, concept note section 4.
#
# ONE INDIRECTION POINT FOR DOMAIN VOCABULARY (REVIEW ITEM R1).
# No domain class IRI is written in this file.  Every one of them arrives as a
# run binding (a ThreadedMaterializer `staticVars` entry) named below:
#
#     v:resultClass   v:qualityClass   v:personClass   v:recordClass
#
# and every node IRI likewise (v:person, v:quality, v:unitIri, v:result,
# v:record, v:timeInstant, v:sourceVersionIri).  Swapping the domain
# vocabulary, or answering R1/R2/R4/R6, is therefore a change to the run
# binding table -- `maps/r4/egfr/egfr-bindings.v1.json` -- and touches no
# schema.
#
# Only SULO 0.2.12 upper-level terms and prov: appear literally.
#
# DR-301 4b/4c: the engine has no id(), a Map variable on a shape-valued
# constraint emits the IRI as a leaf and drops the sub-shape, and only the root
# node of a materialization has a controllable IRI.  Each IRI-identified node
# therefore gets its own entry shape, materialized rooted at that IRI, and
# refers to its neighbours as leaf IRIs.  This is the DR-302 decomposition:
# every triple below is constructed by this schema, and the host only chooses
# roots and unions the passes.

PREFIX sulo: <https://w3id.org/sulo/>
PREFIX prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
PREFIX Map:  <http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#>
PREFIX v:    <https://w3id.org/fhir-sulo/map/egfr/var#>
PREFIX sh:   <https://w3id.org/fhir-sulo/map/egfr/shape#>

start = @sh:EGFRResultNode

# --- the quantity ----------------------------------------------------------
# sulo:hasValue is an owl:FunctionalProperty with domain sulo:InformationObject
# (DR-002 axiom 1), so exactly one value.  sulo:Quantity is subsumed by
# sulo:InformationObject and requires a unit part (DR-002 axiom 2), supplied
# here as the shared UCUM unit IRI.
sh:EGFRResultNode {
  rdf:type [sulo:Quantity] ;
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:resultClass %} ;
  sulo:hasValue xsd:decimal %Map:{ v:value %} ;
  sulo:hasPart  IRI %Map:{ v:unitIri %} ;
  sulo:refersTo IRI %Map:{ v:quality %} ;
  sulo:isFeatureOf IRI %Map:{ v:person %} ;
  sulo:atTime   IRI %Map:{ v:timeInstant %} ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom IRI %Map:{ v:sourceVersionIri %}
}

# --- the quality the quantity refers to ------------------------------------
# R4: sulo:Feature is a disjoint union of Capability/InformationObject/Quality/
# Role (DR-002 axiom 6), so bare Feature leaves the individual unpartitioned.
# The branch is a run binding (v:qualityBranch), defaulting to sulo:Quality per
# the R4 option A recommendation; setting it to sulo:Feature restores the
# concept note's literal text without touching this schema.
sh:EGFRQualityNode {
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:qualityBranch %} ;
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:qualityClass %} ;
  sulo:isFeatureOf IRI %Map:{ v:person %}
}

# --- the person ------------------------------------------------------------
# R6 supplies both the SULO parent (v:personSuloClass) and the domain class
# (v:personClass).  The person IRI itself is the identity service's output,
# never derived from the FHIR reference (concept note section 2).
sh:EGFRPersonNode {
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:personSuloClass %} ;
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:personClass %} ;
  sulo:hasFeature IRI %Map:{ v:quality %}
}

# --- the unit --------------------------------------------------------------
# sulo:Unit is subsumed by sulo:Quantity and sulo:hasPart is reflexive, so a
# unit satisfies its own unit-part requirement (DR-002 axiom 3).
sh:EGFRUnitNode {
  rdf:type [sulo:Unit] ;
  sulo:hasValue xsd:string %Map:{ v:unitCode %}
}

# --- the clinically relevant time ------------------------------------------
# Observation.effective[x], explicitly NOT `issued` or `meta.lastUpdated`
# (concept note section 2).  R5/Q2: whether a TimeInstant carries an explicit
# sulo:Unit is unresolved; the concept note's example graph omits it and so
# does this shape.  Adding it is one triple constraint here plus one run
# binding, not a re-authoring.
sh:EGFRTimeNode {
  rdf:type [sulo:TimeInstant] ;
  sulo:hasValue xsd:dateTime %Map:{ v:effective %}
}

# --- the record layer ------------------------------------------------------
# The FHIR resource and its semantic interpretation are distinct individuals
# and no owl:sameAs joins them (concept note section 2).
#
# R11, answered 2026-09-30. The reviewer: "compositionally, a record could
# indeed be comprised of statements, which could include the recording of
# results. This then captures where the results are located (e.g. the record).
# however, the results are information about the individual - they are
# features of the individual and they also refer to their qualities."
#
# So the record HAS the result as a PART -- where the result is located --
# rather than referring to it. Well-formed: sulo:InformationObject is
# subClassOf (sulo:hasPart only sulo:InformationObject), and a result is a
# sulo:Quantity subClassOf sulo:InformationObject.
sh:EGFRRecordNode {
  rdf:type [sulo:InformationObject] ;
  rdf:type IRI %Map:{ v:recordClass %} ;
  sulo:hasPart IRI %Map:{ v:result %} ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom IRI %Map:{ v:sourceVersionIri %}
}
